        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Brhty",
          "name": "Notes",
          "width": 340,
          "fill": "#fff8dc",
          "cornerRadius": 6,
          "stroke": "#e8d9a0",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 14,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ken4l",
              "name": "Notes title",
              "fill": "#281d1b",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Scene editor: Video section",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "zqjKY",
              "name": "Note 1",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "1. New VIDEO section after Ambience, built like Music: a list of videos with a thumbnail and length, reordered with the arrows, added from a picker or by dragging from the Library.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "N12jni",
              "name": "Note 2",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "2. Switch videos every N minutes: plays one video for N minutes, then the next. Coming back to a video resumes where it left off (the row shows where), or starts it over. 0 plays each to its end.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "we4LQ",
              "name": "Note 3",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "3. Grey values with a link icon follow the project's defaults (Project settings › Video), like Loop and Fade. The reset icon marks a value set for this scene.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "B5vjx",
              "name": "Note 4",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "4. Positions are remembered per video for the session (not saved to the file), so a scene that returns later picks up where it was.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Wj0l9",
              "name": "Note 5",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "5. VIDEO EFFECTS: like the effects pad, chips of videos shown under the sound effects while the scene is in the tapestry.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iSjK0",
              "name": "Note 6",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "6. A scene without videos lets the video below keep playing, or hides it with the switch (like \"Silence the music below\").",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
