        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "EwXMb",
          "name": "Notes",
          "width": 340,
          "fill": "#fff8dc",
          "cornerRadius": 6,
          "stroke": "#e8d9a0",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 14,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "sGl4w",
              "name": "Notes title",
              "fill": "#281d1b",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Video window",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "N5kcyK",
              "name": "Note 1",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "1. A window of its own, meant for a TV or projector the players see. Just the video, filling the window (cropped to fill, or letterboxed: a Preferences choice).",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "R6sTx",
              "name": "Note 2",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "2. Controls appear only while the pointer is over the window, then fade away: which screen it's on, fullscreen, close. The whole top bar is a drag handle: drag it to move the window (the window has no title bar of its own). Double-click it toggles fullscreen.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "s8IZj",
              "name": "Note 3",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "3. The window remembers its screen and fullscreen state, and opens there the next time.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "srLNj",
              "name": "Note 4",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "4. A thin line along the bottom shows when it switches to the next video. Hidden in fullscreen.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "i1kHq",
              "name": "Note 5",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "5. Videos change with a short crossfade (time set in Preferences). The video's own sound is never played.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "l8MNIn",
              "name": "Note 6",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "6. With nothing to show (no scene with videos, a scene hiding them, or Esc), the window turns black. The text only shows outside fullscreen.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
