            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hUEvB",
              "name": "Notes title",
              "fill": "#281d1b",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Convert videos",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vMbyc",
              "name": "Note 1",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "1. Shown when videos that may not play are added: through Add files, by dropping them on the window, or found in the project's video/ folder (copied in with the file manager). The grey line says which.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iplMm",
              "name": "Note 2",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "2. \"May not play\" is decided by ffprobe (part of the ffmpeg we download): anything other than WebM with VP8, VP9 or AV1. MP4/H.264 can play on Linux if the right GStreamer packages are installed, but we can't count on it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hLFjo",
              "name": "Note 3",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "3. The dialog shows the list first with CONVERT 3; once started, each row shows its progress (as here). Closing the dialog keeps it going in the background; the header shows \"Converting 2 videos…\".",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iG3Fj",
              "name": "Note 4",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "4. Unticking a file leaves it as it is.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ICApY",
              "name": "Note 5",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "5. Converted with our ffmpeg to WebM (VP9), keeping the resolution, without sound. The new file replaces the original in every scene that uses it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "OQ3fA",
              "name": "Note 6",
              "fill": "#3a2e28",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "6. Files found in the folder are asked about once per batch, not every 2 seconds: if several arrive together they're listed together.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
